      "text": "Nvidia did not fall alone. The S&P 500 ended Friday at 6,902, below the 7,000 level, according to Motley Fool, and closing prices put its day at −3.7%. Reuters noted the index had already fallen for a fifth straight day by Wednesday.\n\nOther chipmakers fell with Nvidia. Broadcom dropped 12.12% in Motley Fool's count, while closing prices put it at −12.2%. AMD lost 13.26% to $424.32, with concerns about firmware security and alleged ties to blacklisted Chinese companies in the mix. Micron was down 12.03% at midday. The chip index (SOX) changed −10.7% on Friday.\n\nRates added pressure. Reuters reported on Nov 17 that markets priced a near-certain 95.4% chance of a 25-basis-point Fed rate increase in December, according to CME's FedWatch tool. Bloomberg reported that minutes of the Fed's October meeting showed nearly all officials agreed they would likely have to raise rates in the months ahead. The 10-year Treasury yield stood at 5.04% at midday Friday, down three basis points.\n\nNvidia was already down more than 6% on Friday before its own report landed, per Reuters. The group's weakness came first.",
