  "next_text": "Next week is short. US markets close Thursday, Nov 26, for Thanksgiving, so most of the news lands Monday through Wednesday.\n\nMonday brings the preliminary S&P manufacturing PMI for November at 9:45 ET, and Zoom reports after the close. Tuesday has Conference Board consumer confidence at 10:00 ET. Dell, Workday and HP report after the close. Dell guided fiscal Q3 revenue of $49.0 billion, up 81%, so results near that figure would match its own forecast, and a gap in either direction would stand out.\n\nWednesday is the heaviest data day. The October PCE price index, consumer spending and the second estimate of Q3 GDP all arrive at 8:30 ET. Markets already priced a 95.4% chance of a December Fed increase as of Nov 17. Inflation data that firms up that view would fit the pricing. A softer reading would leave the December decision less settled.\n\nOne Nvidia item has no date yet. The company said its Form 10-Q would be filed in the coming weeks. Nothing in the sources says when, so the filing could arrive in any of the days ahead.",
